    "body": "Actual consumer failure with lino-objects-codec0.9.0 and Node22.23.0, while verifying a full saved Lazada associative case. The codec successfully emitted valid readable Links Notation, but cannot read it back.\n\nThe discovery-publication-source document contains1,764 historical proof records,144,497,741 UTF8 bytes, content SHA25633288f6b43e93e619e92eb622383da322ba8bb6022503dc6e8faa6f9c5a088a4 (gzip24,975,140 bytes). A smaller56,510,065-byte cache notation is also present. Source JSON, compressed/uncompressed hashes and binary frames remain intact.\n\nActual stack:\n```\nRangeError: Invalid array length\n at Function.from (<anonymous>)\n at tokenize (.../lino-objects-codec/src/readable.js:582:23)\n at Module.decode (.../src/readable.js:224:18)\n at ObjectCodec.decode (.../src/codec.js:200:21)\n at decode (.../src/codec.js:784:24)\n```\n\n`tokenize` calls `Array.from(text)` before scanning, multiplying memory use and reaching V8 backing-array limits for a valid large document. A narrow consumer workaround uses direct string indexing and string slices instead of the character array and corresponding slice/join calls. ASCII delimiters and complete Unicode text/quote runs must round-trip. The separate escaped-payload decoder also materializes arrays and deserves bounded Unicode/UTF8 processing for giant single values.\n\nPlease support decoding valid large documents without whole-document character arrays, preserve exact encoded/decoded JSON and Unicode/quote/escaped-marker behavior, and add a realistic regression. The consumer will keep verifying every saved notation record against JSON and binary conversion, not skip decode or remove history. A public fixed/failed archive receipt and consumer workaround link will follow after full validation and commit. No marketplace requests are needed to reproduce.\n",
